Seam: the allowlist in
      chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc and its
      target's deps in chrome/browser/extensions/BUILD.gn, and the About
      page's element and template in
      chrome/browser/resources/settings/about_page/.
Why: the reader has to be able to choose how updates arrive. The setting
     belongs to the whole browser rather than to a profile, and the settings
     page may only read and write a setting that is named in the allowlist.
     The row itself is a dropdown bound to that setting by name, placed under
     the update status it governs; its label and choices come from the
     browser, through patch 0262.
Delegates to: arcium/browser/update/update_preference.h for the setting's
     name. The page's markup is a resource keyed by file name and the
     allowlist is a registration table of the same kind, so neither can be
     moved into arcium/; the row's text and values are built in
     arcium/ui/browser/update_settings.cc.

